From c344e457928bb84349880cd2814551b3d75bf00a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ant=C3=B3nio=20Sarmento?= <Keyaku@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 18:31:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] vold: drop MS_DIRSYNC for exfat public volumes

Deleting a large directory tree from the microSD through the Files app
silently failed: the notification ran and the folder was still there.

DocumentsUI hands ExternalStorageProvider the tree root in a single
deleteDocument call, and FileSystemProvider recurses the whole tree
inside that one binder transaction. With MS_DIRSYNC every directory
entry costs a synchronous flush to the card, so a 24k-entry tree takes
minutes; AMS declares the provider unresponsive ("ContentProvider not
responding"), kills it mid-walk, and nothing propagates back to the
caller.

Measured on the shipped card, 2000 empty files: unlink 10.54s with
MS_DIRSYNC, 0.04s without. Creation drops 18.16s to 1.97s.

The flag is the FAT-family substitute for a journal, so this is a
deliberate divergence from upstream (AOSP master and LineageOS both set
it). It costs less than it looks: MS_DIRSYNC covers directory metadata
only, file contents are buffered either way, so a hot eject was already
unsafe. Upstream itself omits the flag for adopted storage on the same
physically ejectable card. The exfat driver's own delayed_meta batching
stays in effect, and errors=remount-ro still guards a surprise removal.

Changes:
- `Exfat.cpp`: drop `MS_DIRSYNC` from the mount flags, leaving `Vfat.cpp` and `Ntfs.cpp` on upstream behavior

Change-Id: Ib9f089b8f6f3bcd2842d9b9c0d6d7cf696799732
---
 fs/Exfat.cpp | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/fs/Exfat.cpp b/fs/Exfat.cpp
index 34f10240..a57e55af 100644
--- a/fs/Exfat.cpp
+++ b/fs/Exfat.cpp
@@ -57,7 +57,11 @@ status_t Check(const std::string& source) {
 
 status_t Mount(const std::string& source, const std::string& target, int ownerUid, int ownerGid,
                int permMask) {
-    int mountFlags = MS_NODEV | MS_NOSUID | MS_DIRSYNC | MS_NOATIME | MS_NOEXEC;
+    // No MS_DIRSYNC: the exfat driver already batches FAT/bitmap metadata
+    // (delayed_meta), and a synchronous flush per directory entry makes a
+    // large recursive delete take minutes, long enough for the framework to
+    // kill ExternalStorageProvider mid-walk.
+    int mountFlags = MS_NODEV | MS_NOSUID | MS_NOATIME | MS_NOEXEC;
     auto mountData = android::base::StringPrintf("uid=%d,gid=%d,fmask=%o,dmask=%o", ownerUid,
                                                  ownerGid, permMask, permMask);
 
